    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>Crandall University is in Canada, New Brunswick. It is a non-profit Christian Liberal Arts institution. Currently, the establishment offers higher education courses at Bachelors and Masters levels. The university also provides programs for subjects such as Education, Business and Science.<br><br>The institution also has a small intake of students, around 1,000. As a result, an intimate, close and welcoming community exists on campus with small classes taking place. There are also plenty of extracurricular activities and options available on and off campus.</p><p>In its 200-acre campus, Crandall provides students with top-level higher-education facilities. Also, the Baptist Heritage Center has various specialist materials, such as paintings, furniture, service materials and musical instruments.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Crandall University has an active and welcoming campus. Students are also encouraged to become part of the universitys community through various clubs, organisations or sports teams.<br><br>Many faith-based clubs are available for students as the university stays true to its Christian roots. As a result, students can participate in various services and discussion clubs. Also, students can take part in voluntary activities that give back to the campus and the local community. Alternatively, Crandall has many other clubs, including soccer, basketball, boxing, cross country and more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>Currently, students attending Crandall can find on-campus accommodation options. The university has dedicated halls of residence for undergraduate and postgraduate students.&nbsp;</p><p>First, undergraduate students can apply for accommodation in the Colburne House halls. There is a lively and inclusive student community with various shared and private accommodations. However, postgraduate students can stay in the Mitton Court halls. This residence provides shared apartment options for students, who share a living space and other facilities.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>Students can access the main library on campus, where they can find resources and materials for all courses.</p>",
